{{also|har|hār|hår|hár|hær}}
==Swedish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/hæːr/|lang=sv}}
* {{audio|sv-här.ogg|Audio}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|sv}} {{term|hér|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|sv}} {{recons|hē₂r|lang=gem-pro}}.

====Adverb====
{{head|sv|adverb}}

# [[here]]; at this time ''or'' at this place
#: '''''Här''' är den.''
#:: Here it is.

=====Usage notes=====
* In several compounds (''[[härkomst]], [[härledning]], ...''), it is also used like the German adverb {{term|lang=de|her||here, to this place}}, which would translate to Swedish {{term|lang=sv|hit||here, to this place}}, rather than ''här''.

=====Antonyms=====
* [[där]]

=====See also=====
* [[dit]]
* [[hädan]]
* [[hän]]
* [[hit]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|non|sv}} {{term|herr|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|sv}} {{recons|harjaz|lang=gem-pro}}.

====Noun====
{{sv-noun|c}}

# {{context|historical|lang=sv}} a land [[army]]
#: '''''Härarna''' drabbade samman tidigt på morgonen.''
#:: The '''armies''' [[clash]]ed in the early morning.

